{
  "_README": [
    "This is a PLACEHOLDER, not a working Firebase config.",
    "",
    "This project does not ship a shared google-services.json on purpose:",
    "Realtime Database data belongs to a specific Firebase project, so every",
    "developer should point at their OWN Firebase project (or one they have",
    "been explicitly added to).",
    "",
    "Setup:",
    "  1. Create a Firebase project at https://console.firebase.google.com",
    "  2. Add an Android app with package name: com.example.student_registration",
    "     (it must match applicationId in app/build.gradle.kts exactly)",
    "  3. Enable Realtime Database and create the database",
    "  4. Download google-services.json and place it at: app/google-services.json",
    "     (this file is gitignored, so it will not be committed)",
    "  5. Rebuild the app.",
    "",
    "If you see 'File google-services.json is missing' at build time, step 4.",
    "If the app crashes with 'Failed to get app instance' at runtime, the file is",
    "present but does not contain a client entry for the app's package name."
  ],
  "project_info": {
    "project_number": "000000000000",
    "project_id": "your-firebase-project-id",
    "storage_bucket": "your-firebase-project-id.appspot.com"
  },
  "client": [
    {
      "client_info": {
        "mobilesdk_app_id": "1:000000000000:android:0000000000000000000000",
        "android_client_info": {
          "package_name": "com.example.student_registration"
        }
      },
      "oauth_client": [],
      "api_key": [
        {
          "current_key": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_API_KEY"
        }
      ],
      "services": {
        "appinvite_service": {
          "other_platform_oauth_client": []
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "configuration_version": "1"
}
